2. Auto Update Agent: Built From Scratch

A major contribution was the development and continuous enhancement of the Auto Update Agent.

The objective of the agent is to automatically identify assets impacted by a claim change and update the relevant content while maintaining document traceability and review information.

The workflow developed around the agent includes:

Receiving the claim that has been changed.
Identifying documents associated with that claim.
Retrieving document and annotation information.
Locating the claim-related content inside the asset.
Using contextual information and LLM reasoning where appropriate.
Generating the updated content.
Updating the actual source asset.
Creating the correct new document version.
Migrating/recreating necessary annotations.
Maintaining linkage between the previous and newly created document versions.
Generating information necessary for reviewers to compare changes.

Particular attention was given to ensuring that an update does not accidentally create multiple document versions when several annotations belonging to the same asset are processed.

This required restructuring the update flow so that document processing and uploading happen at the appropriate level rather than blindly creating a new Veeva version for every annotation.

