5. HTML Claim Auto-Update Workflow

The initial Auto Update functionality primarily operated on HTML-based assets.

The workflow identifies the HTML sentence associated with the relevant annotation and uses the previous and newly approved versions of the claim to determine how that particular sentence should change.

One particularly useful aspect of the HTML flow was its ability to use the relevant contextual sentence instead of relying only on exact full-string equality.

This became the reference architecture when expanding the same Auto Update capability to Word and PowerPoint documents.

6. Extending Auto Update to DOCX Documents

One of the major recent enhancements was adding support for Microsoft Word (DOCX) assets.

A key issue encountered was that the claim stored in the system and the actual sentence appearing inside the Word document are frequently not identical strings.

For example, an approved claim may be incorporated into a longer marketing sentence or contain slightly different contextual wording.

Therefore, simple logic such as:

Plain Text
if document_text == old_claim
